message.content:
You are Koda. Build **Track B of Sprint 3 — Calendar enhancements** for InkOS at `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/InkOS`.

## Scope (TRACK B ONLY — do not touch workers, today, or inbox)

Three visual additions to the existing FullCalendar implementation:

1. **Deposit status dots** on event cards (red = unpaid required deposit, green = paid)
2. **Project chain icon** on events linked to a Project (from Sprint 1)
3. **Guest artist residency bars** — horizontal bars above the day/week grid showing current/upcoming guest-artist engagements

## CONTEXT — read first

- **CLAUDE.md** at project root — forbidden list
- **Plan Section B1** in `/Users/yashbaldha/.claude/plans/so-we-made-detailed-glistening-frost.md`
- **Competitor pattern (TattooGenda):** "Green dot = paid, red dot = deposit pending." Guest spots shown as horizontal bars.
- **Current calendar:** `components/calendar/CalendarView.tsx` + `app/(app)/calendar/CalendarPageClient.tsx` + `app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx`. Uses FullCalendar v6 (dayGrid, timeGrid, list, interaction plugins). Events render with `eventContent` callback. Status already has CSS classes `status-{pending|confirmed|...}`.
- **Projects (Sprint 1) added:** `bookings.project_id` + `bookings.session_number`. When set, show a link icon that routes to `/projects/[project_id]`.
- **Guest artists:** `guest_artist_engagements` table with `start_date`, `end_date`, `artist_id`. Read existing usage (probably in `app/(app)/artists/` or `app/(app)/guest-artists/`) for reference.

## 1. Deposit dots

In `components/calendar/CalendarView.tsx` `eventContent` renderer:
- Check `booking.deposit_cents > 0` AND `booking.deposit_paid`
- If deposit_cents = 0: no dot
- If deposit_cents > 0 AND deposit_paid: green 6px dot in top-right of event card (positioned absolute)
- If deposit_cents > 0 AND !deposit_paid: red 6px dot with subtle pulse animation
- Use design tokens from `app/globals.css`: `var(--color-success)` (green) and `var(--color-destructive)` (red)
- Add `title` attr for a11y: "Deposit paid" / "Deposit pending"

CSS additions in `app/globals.css`:
```css
.fc-event .deposit-dot {
  position: absolute;
  top: 4px;
  right: 4px;
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1.5px var(--color-card);
  z-index: 2;
}
.fc-event .deposit-dot.paid { background: var(--color-success); }
.fc-event .deposit-dot.unpaid { 
  background: var(--color-destructive);
  animation: deposit-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes deposit-pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: 0.6; }
}
```

## 2. Project chain icon

In the same `eventContent` renderer:
- If `booking.project_id` is not null, render a small link/chain glyph (use `Link2` from `lucide-react` at 10px)
- Position: bottom-right of event card (absolute)
- On click (via `extendedProps` or a separate anchor): stop propagation, navigate to `/projects/[project_id]` using `useRouter().push()`
- Hover tooltip: "Part of project: {project name} · Session {session_number}"
- To fetch project name efficiently: extend the booking query in `CalendarPageClient.tsx` or wherever bookings are fetched to join `projects(name)` — do it in one query.

CSS:
```css
.fc-event .project-icon {
  position: absolute;
  bottom: 4px;
  right: 4px;
  opacity: 0.75;
  z-index: 2;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.fc-event .project-icon:hover { opacity: 1; }
```

## 3. Guest artist residency bars

New component `components/calendar/GuestArtistStrip.tsx`:
- Fetches guest_artist_engagements where start_date <= viewEnd AND end_date >= viewStart
- Renders horizontal strip above calendar grid
- One row per active engagement, spans the dates visually (calendar-day-width aware — use % positioning based on days-in-view)
- Artist name + avatar on left; dates on right
- Click → popover showing full engagement details + portfolio link + "Book with guest artist" CTA
- Sticky position just below calendar toolbar
- Show/hide toggle (persistent in localStorage as `calendar-guest-strip-visible`, default true)
- Empty state: do not render if no engagements in view

Wire into `CalendarPageClient.tsx`:
- Pass viewStart/viewEnd from FullCalendar view change callback
- Pass engagements data fetched server-side (or via a lightweight `/api/guest-artists/engagements?start=X&end=Y` route if cleaner)

CSS for `GuestArtistStrip`:
```css
.guest-artist-strip {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 4px;
  padding: 8px 12px;
  background: var(--color-muted);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 10;
}
.guest-artist-bar {
  position: relative;
  height: 28px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 0 10px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  /* Use one of the artist colors from the palette (--color-artist-N) */
}
```

Use existing artist palette `--color-artist-1` through `--color-artist-10` (see `app/globals.css`).

## 4. Role-aware default view

Bonus (if time allows): the calendar page should respect role:
- Owner/admin: default `filterArtistIds` = []  (all chairs)
- Artist: default `filterArtistIds` = [current artist's id]  (my chair only)
- Receptionist: default `filterArtistIds` = []  (all chairs) + add "Check-in focus" toggle (shows only today's pending check-ins)

Pull current artist via `getActiveStudio()` + a `artists.profile_id = user.id` lookup.

## Quality gates

- `pnpm typecheck` clean
- `pnpm build` clean
- No `any`, no `console.log`
- All new queries use `studioId` scoping
- Visual test at 375px mobile viewport (calendar responsive)
- Dark mode — the dots and bars should use CSS variables that adapt

## Report

- Files modified (list with line ranges)
- New components created
- Screenshot-worthy changes (what to visually verify in dev)
- Typecheck + build results

